const CHANGELOG=[
  {date:"2026-08-21",title:"Alpha 2.11 accuracy pass: schemes, provenance and honest damping",items:["Method now states how heavily the early years are damped and by how much: competition is scaled 60x in 2009 tapering to 1x from 2014, which is a 0.02x effect on 2009 yield and 0.99x from 2024, and the tab shows the live factor for your own fleet and date.","Said plainly that the ASIC era runs the real block-probability arithmetic and the CPU and GPU eras do not, and that this is a balance decision rather than a historical claim.","Solo mining no longer says shares submitted, because solo against your own node submits nothing anywhere; it now reads difficulty-1 shares found, and shares submitted only when pool mining.","Your best share is now reconciled with the blocks you actually found: solo, it crosses network difficulty on exactly the days you find a block and never on the days you do not.","Pool payout schemes are now modelled rather than assumed: FPPS, PPS, PPS+, PPLNS and OCEAN TIDES differ in whether transaction fees reach you and who carries the variance.","Pool fees corrected to real headline rates — AntPool 4%, F2Pool 2.5%, Deepbit 3% PPS, ViaBTC 2% PPS+, Slush 2%, BTC.com 1.5%, Foundry and MARA and OCEAN 0%.","A pay-per-share pool now costs more than its fee suggests: at mid-2023 fee levels a 3% PPS pool lands 9.8% behind the best option, because the transaction fees never reach you.","Fixed the Pools tab charging the pool fee twice in its expected-net-BTC figure.","Selecting a pool you are not eligible for no longer mines solo in silence while the tab still says pool; it fails over explicitly and says why.","Method now shows where every recorded series comes from, read live from the data bundle: the source, the through-date, the row counts and how each series was derived.","Documented that your own hash rate does move your odds through the share formula — below about 1% of the network doubling your fleet doubles your blocks, and at 2.5% share per-machine yield is 12% lower.","Corrected the claim that no BTC/USD price existed before Mt. Gox: New Liberty Standard quoted a rate from October 2009 and bitcoinmarket.com ran from March 2010.","Split the simulation engine into operator, maintenance, pools and notification modules so it fits inside the project's own module-size limit."]},
  {date:"2026-08-21",title:"Alpha 2.11 steadier repaints and manual intervention",items:["The Mine tab no longer kicks the page down when a fault notification arrives: the rebuild and its enhancement now happen in one task, so the browser never paints the short un-enhanced tab first.","Repaints now anchor on the card you are actually reading, keyed to its heading, so a fault row or the bench panel appearing above your position no longer shifts everything under you.","Ordering spare parts patches the Mine tab instead of rebuilding the whole page, which is what jumped the view down to miner selection.","High speeds now repaint less often rather than more — every 600ms at 16x instead of 300ms — and every queued repaint is aligned to the display refresh, which removes the jitter.","The bad-event screen shake is throttled to once every four seconds; the red flash still fires each time, so a burst of faults no longer throws the page around.","When every field technician is already committed to another repair, the next job now falls to you to complete by hand rather than being refused, provided the parts are in stock.","A self-serviced job no longer consumes technician capacity, so your own bench and a full crew can work in parallel.","The Mine floor bench panel now appears whenever no technician is free, not only when none are hired."]},
  {date:"2026-08-21",title:"Alpha 2.11 operator XP, levels and the best share",items:["Added a permanent operator experience bar to the header, with the running level, XP to the next level and your best share difficulty.","XP is earned from shares submitted, new best-share difficulty records, machines commissioned and repairs completed, with a 50% bonus on repairs you carry out yourself.","Share XP is logarithmic in hash rate, so a 2009 laptop earns roughly 8 XP a day and a 324 PH/s campus roughly 51 — a six-fold spread across eleven orders of magnitude of fleet size.","Your best share difficulty is now tracked and announced when you beat it by a wide margin: the number solo miners actually watch, drawn from a heavy-tailed distribution so it climbs in rare jumps.","Levels need 60 x (N-1) squared cumulative XP and grant skill points on a decelerating schedule — every level to 6, then every second to 20, then every fourth — about 22 points across a long campaign.","Peak operator level now contributes up to 60 mastery points to the Operator Score, taken out of the era-performance allocation, which drops from 800 to 740 so the total stays at 1,000.","XP augments the Operator Score rather than replacing it: XP only ever rises, so the Score keeps its era weighting and its penalties for bridge loans and receivership.","The Operator Score card now shows your level, mastery points, best share, shares submitted and a breakdown of XP by source.","On narrow screens the XP bar becomes a hairline progress strip along the bottom of the header instead of competing for width."]},
  {date:"2026-08-21",title:"Alpha 2.11 self-sufficiency: free labour, bench skills & dismissals",items:["Servicing your own fleet no longer costs fiat labour — a self-serviced job charges you for parts and nothing else. Technician crews are still paid.","Fumbling your own repair can now damage the machine: a wrong bolt, a mismatched connector pair or an over-torque past spec can cost several points of condition and sometimes break a second part outright.","That damage risk falls sharply with practice on that specific hardware type, from roughly 40% on a machine you have never opened down to a 2% floor.","Added Bench repair skills: cuts the chance of damaging a machine you are working on to 40% of its value.","Added Parts sourcing: every spare part costs 20% less.","Added Supply-chain contacts: spare-part orders arrive 40% sooner, supply shock included.","Added Practised hands: a familiar repair can complete itself with no puzzle at all, from 20% after one repair of that type up to a capped 85% after eight.","None of the four self-help skills require a facility tier, so a solo operator can stay self-sufficient instead of being pushed into hiring.","A new bench panel on the Mine floor shows completed repairs, current damage risk and auto-finish odds for every hardware type you own.","Staff can now be dismissed: salary stops immediately and one month's notice is added to that month's accrued bill.","A technician committed to a running repair cannot be dismissed until that job clears, and losing your last technician switches auto-repair back off."]},
  {date:"2026-08-21",title:"Alpha 2.11 exposure warnings, per-site floors & hands-on servicing",items:["Four historical collapses now warn you in advance, but only while you are actually exposed: Mt. Gox halting bitcoin withdrawals on 07 Feb 2014, a bank freezing QuadrigaCX's processor funds on 09 Oct 2018, the leaked Alameda balance sheet on 02 Nov 2022, and Beijing naming Bitcoin mining on 21 May 2021.","Each warning fires a one-time amber toast and ledger entry, then holds a banner showing the exact exposed balance or region until you withdraw, relocate, or the real event arrives.","Bitfinex's 2016 hack and Kazakhstan's 2022 internet shutdown are deliberately excluded because neither had a genuine public advance warning, and ignoring a warning leaves the real event's effect completely unchanged.","You now service your own fleet by hand until field technicians are hired: the Work-stage repair puzzle belongs to jobs you run yourself, and a hired crew completes its own work without handing it back to you.","Repair-puzzle state is now prepared when the job is created, so the puzzle can no longer appear with controls that do nothing until the clock advances.","Fixed a repair loop where a replaced part immediately re-faulted: a completed part swap now clears that part's fault count outright and restores condition above the 65% offline threshold with headroom against the same tick's wear.","Spare parts split from five shared items into nine era-scaled ones — a $15 laptop fan, $45 120mm case fan and $55 ASIC blower, plus $180 early, $480 mid-generation and $900 high-density hashboards chosen by each machine's era and release date.","Every facility tier now has its own mining-floor illustration, from a domestic spare room and a garage roller shutter through three-phase trade units, warehouse containment and substations to container yards, hydro penstocks and transmission switchyards.","All nine spare parts now have their own drawings instead of sharing five, so a laptop blower, a case fan and an industrial ASIC blower are told apart at a glance.","The Bitcoin Faucet popup now patches the page like a toast instead of forcing a full re-render, removing the scroll jump it caused.","The solo ledger label now reads Block reward (today) because the logged amount is the day's total, not one block's subsidy.","The Dashboard mempool visualisation now pauses with the simulation instead of animating while the clock is stopped.","The first skill point now arrives at 5 knowledge instead of 9, with later points still every 3.","Moved facility and spare-part illustration into its own module to keep the fleet view inside the agreed file-size ceiling."]},
  {date:"2026-08-18",title:"Alpha 2.10 fleet labour, exchange trading & risk",items:["Repairs now move through six labour stages — power down, disconnect, work, reconnect, fit & rack, stability check — each with its own complication chance, reduced by the new Field service technique skill.","Outside contractors now cover only one job at a time fleet-wide when no technician is on payroll; a second attempt is blocked until that job clears.","An unrepaired, unattended fault has a small daily chance to spread to a second part instead of sitting inert.","Added an overdrive toggle: +15% hash and +25% power draw at the cost of sharply higher wear and fault risk, able to push a facility over its own electrical capacity.","Surfaced the previously invisible load-based power-rate penalty on the Energy tariff desk and Mine's electrical capacity tile.","The forced BTC settlement rescue no longer executes a one-click sale: it routes to Market, where covering the shortfall means depositing to a real exchange and selling there, with the settlement clearing itself once cash covers it.","Redesigned every exchange into a trade ticket: a bid/ask quote, a branded monogram, and independent buy/sell sizing instead of one shared percentage slider.","Fixed the dashboard's displayed network hashrate to match the effective competitive figure mining odds are actually computed against, instead of the sparse raw recorded curve.","Bad events (faults, outages, compromises, migration incidents, settlement shortfalls) now trigger a brief red screen flash and shake.","Reduced the starter region's internet bill from $75/mo to $25/mo."]},
  {date:"2026-08-16",title:"Alpha 2.9 stabilisation & modular rebuild",items:["Replaced arbitrary opening liquidity with Hard, Medium, Easy and Very easy campaign modes.","Transaction displays now preserve tiny non-zero amounts and expose invalid quotes instead of presenting them as zero.","The Mine tab now uses one dollar-purchase button per miner, with unique batch quantities selected beside it.","Separated static data, simulation, actions, tab views, enhancements, rendering, events and styling into bounded files with structural regression checks.","Expanded the Method tab with opening-mode, quote-sizing, procurement, settlement and Operator Score mechanics."]},
  {date:"2026-08-15",title:"Alpha 2.9 ASIC release intelligence",items:["Every ASIC and hydro-ASIC release now pauses the timeline with a decision briefing containing physical hashrate, input power and joules per terahash.","Release alerts quantify the step change from the prior mining generation: throughput multiple, efficiency gain, equal-hash power demand and monthly energy-cost impact at the active site tariff.","A 1,000-machine flexible-load scenario translates each generation into megawatts, monthly energy and one-hour demand-response potential.","The Mine tab now retains an ASIC efficiency and controllable-load timeline so generation changes can be compared after their launch alerts are dismissed."]},
  {date:"2026-08-15",title:"Alpha 2.8 transaction confirmations",items:["Added an explicit review modal before market, ETF, Strategy security, miner and fleet-liquidation purchases or sales can execute.","Every confirmation freezes the simulation quote and places the asset or hardware given beside the cash, BTC, shares or equipment received.","Percentage basis, reference or unit price, fees and resulting balances are shown before commitment; cancelling restores the prior timeline speed without changing state.","Confirmation uses the same underlying calculations as execution so the review and completed transaction remain aligned."]},
  {date:"2026-08-15",title:"Alpha 2.7 configurable capital & precise orders",items:["Added a pre-run liquidity control from $1,500 to $250,000, with a broad slider and exact numeric override.","Every market venue now has a persistent 1–100% transaction-size control with slider, exact percentage entry and 1%, 25%, 50% and 100% snaps.","Deposit, withdraw, buy and sell are now separate confirmation buttons that use the displayed percentage and state clearly which source balance it applies to.","Opening liquidity and percentage-sized transactions are captured by the permanent activity ledger."]},
  {date:"2026-08-15",title:"Alpha 2.6 activity ledger & fleet liquidity",items:["Added a permanent, filterable transaction and action history with post-action cash, self-held BTC, fleet hash and market-price snapshots.","Existing saves migrate their retained recent log; all new trades, rewards, bills, fleet changes, custody moves and operational decisions remain in the ledger.","Added a bill-aware fleet liquidation desk that previews the exact miners and proceeds needed to reach a chosen fiat target while protecting stronger hash margin first.","Monthly settlement rescue now identifies the specific fleet sale and expected cash proceeds before the player commits."]},
  {date:"2026-08-15",title:"Alpha 2.5 recorded network economics",items:["Replaced 118 price anchors with 5,870 daily BTC/USD observations while retaining the pre-market discovery points.","Mining yield now follows 920 daily difficulty states reconstructed from recorded hashrate and block count instead of inferring difficulty from quarterly interpolation.","Transaction fees now use a seven-day network mean across 1,009 anchors, replacing five flat fee eras and exposing real fee-market cycles in profitability.","Network hashrate, transaction activity and block height now use smoothed or cumulative recorded series, with their measurement windows labelled in the live dashboard."]},
  {date:"2026-08-15",title:"Alpha 2.4 obligations & connectivity",items:["Added a rolling three-settlement obligations timeline with an itemized forecast for energy, rent, internet, payroll, insurance, node services and finance interest.","Internet is now a real jurisdiction-priced operating cost with local fixed broadband, dual-SIM cellular failover and business fibre/SLA choices.","Connectivity plans trade monthly cost and outage resilience against mining propagation performance, while facility scale increases bandwidth costs.","Rebalanced the technology tree with escalating point costs, historical dates, facility prerequisites and smaller early multipliers."]},
  {date:"2026-08-15",title:"Alpha 2.3 game-first economy",items:["Replaced the passive BTC leaderboard with a 1,000-point Operator Score built from solvency, profitability, uptime, competitiveness, milestones, custody and resilience.","Added treasury policies that can HODL, sell a chosen share of monthly mining production or automatically sell only enough BTC to cover settlement.","Monthly shortfalls now pause the clock for an explicit rescue decision: sell self-held BTC, liquidate inefficient miners, use costly bridge finance or enter receivership.","Repeated receivership can end the scored campaign, preventing an insolvent offline fleet from coasting to victory while preserving sandbox continuation.","Growth finance can now be supported by recent mining revenue as well as fiat collateral, allowing a profitable operator to fund the next hardware generation."]},
  {date:"2026-08-09",title:"Clearer finance and energy ownership",items:["Removed power-contract selection from the shared operating-strategy card, leaving tariff decisions exclusively in the Energy tab.","Project finance now appears as unavailable until industrial mining credit emerges in 2014, then calculates remaining capacity strictly from eligible unborrowed fiat.","Unavailable growth funding is visibly disabled and displays the exact time or collateral requirement instead of relying on a clickable button and follow-up toast.","Financing exposure now reports true eligible collateral and remaining borrowing capacity, including a genuine zero balance rather than a display-only floor."]},
  {date:"2026-08-09",title:"Detailed American flag artwork",items:["Rebuilt the North America flag SVG with thirteen alternating red and white stripes instead of a blue field with red bars.","Added a compact fifty-dot white star field to the blue canton so the flag remains recognizable at both facility-card and header sizes."]},
  {date:"2026-08-09",title:"Node catch-up and geographic redundancy",items:["Full nodes now accumulate a modelled block backlog while they are powered down, disconnected or short of storage, then visibly catch up before returning to the chain tip.","Laptop, dedicated and hardened deployments synchronize at different rates, teaching that a node can be running without yet being current.","A geographically independent backup node becomes available in 2018, performs its own initial synchronization and can preserve verification during a primary-site power, policy or connectivity failure.","Primary and backup nodes now expose separate sync state, failure reasons, verification paths and operating overhead; remote redundancy protects validation continuity but does not provide local block-template, relay or Lightning services."]},
  {date:"2026-08-09",title:"Laptop-first full-node progression",items:["Bitcoin Core now begins on the Basic laptop as an archival full node instead of incorrectly presenting the starting wallet as SPV-only.","Laptop verification follows the mining laptop's power and hardware state; a dedicated full node remains online when miners are deliberately shut down, while site outages, arrears and insufficient storage still matter.","Reframed the paid node purchase as a dedicated full-node appliance, retained the hardened relay tier and added live verification coverage, continuity and offline-reason UX.","Laptop nodes can switch between archival and pruned profiles, while Lightning still requires a continuously operated dedicated node."]},
  {date:"2026-08-09",title:"Complete fleet artwork and clear status lights",items:["The permanent Basic laptop now receives its hardware SVG in the Mine catalogue, matching every purchasable miner card.","Fleet-header quantity badges moved to the upper-left so they no longer cover the upper-right hardware-status indicator.","Reduced the solid green online light diameter by one-third for a cleaner status treatment."]},
  {date:"2026-08-09",title:"Bitcoin favicon",items:["Added a dedicated Bitcoin-orange browser favicon with a white ₿ mark for tabs, bookmarks and installed shortcuts."]},
  {date:"2026-08-09",title:"Earned cash-reserve milestone",items:["The Six-month cash reserve milestone no longer triggers from the tiny home-office bill against untouched starting cash.","Qualification now requires a tier 2 facility or larger, 180 actual mining-uptime days, no grid arrears and six months of unborrowed fiat against full operating and project-finance costs.","Finance now shows the next unmet reserve requirement so the milestone is demanding but legible."]},
  {date:"2026-08-09",title:"Alpha 2.2 balance and profitability desk",items:["Added a live Mine profitability desk showing marginal BTC and fiat revenue, energy cost, hash margin, production cost, payback and site-capacity use for each available miner.","The desk distinguishes owned fleets from one-unit purchase candidates and flags hardware whose shutdown would improve cash margin.","Added six deterministic era benchmark scenarios to the Method tab so network share, capacity, runway and solvency assumptions can be regression-checked as the game evolves.","Aligned heat-reuse savings with the daily bill ledger so the Mine desk, monthly forecast and actual settlement use the same energy calculation."]},
  {date:"2026-08-09",title:"Realistic network competition",items:["Early mining payouts now include a modelled population of unseen hobbyists around the sparse historical hashrate estimates.","The rest of the network responds as the player's fleet scales, preventing one operation from unrealistically reaching dominant global share.","Dashboard share and payout calculations now use the same effective-competition model while the header retains the stored historical hashrate baseline."]},
  {date:"2026-08-09",title:"Live Mine desk",items:["Opening Mine no longer pauses the historical timeline or changes the selected simulation speed.","Miner prices and buy-max limits refresh while the Mine tab remains open.","Hardware purchases, sales and activations now redraw only the Mine content and live header instead of rebuilding the entire game screen."]},
  {date:"2026-08-09",title:"Clear compact miner pricing",items:["Miner purchase and resale controls now show total transaction values instead of presenting an unexplained machine count in parentheses.","Large fiat and bitcoin amounts use consistent lowercase k, m, b and t suffixes.","Buy-max labels now state both the compact total price and the number of miners, with BTC maximums also respecting remaining facility capacity."]},
  {date:"2026-08-09",title:"Facility-gated staffing",items:["Staff recruitment now requires a tier 3 Light industrial unit or any larger facility.","Finance explains the facility requirement and keeps every hire action disabled until it is met.","Existing employees remain on payroll if an established operation later relocates to a smaller site."]},
  {date:"2026-08-09",title:"ETF chronology and the Winklevoss arc",items:["Finance now keeps spot Bitcoin ETF exposure completely hidden until the U.S. products launch on 10 January 2024.","Added the SEC's 10 March 2017 rejection of the Winklevoss Bitcoin Trust to the historical story.","Added the Winklevoss Capital purchase of a 45% stake in Real Bedford FC after the deal was finalised in February 2025."]},
  {date:"2026-08-09",title:"Miner delivery, activation and status art",items:["Delivered miners now enter staged inventory and require explicit activation in Mine before they hash.","Miner artwork now shows green online lights, yellow electrical warnings, red hardware-fault flames and configuration warnings.","Corrected the quad-core tower artwork and enlarged the glowing fleet illustrations in the Mine header."]},
  {date:"2026-08-09",title:"Live learning progress",items:["Learning day and percentage counters now update on every simulation tick while the Learn tab is open.","Completion immediately refreshes the Learn view so knowledge checks and completed states appear without changing tabs."]},
  {date:"2026-08-09",title:"Progressive historical narrative",items:["Added era-aware narrative copy across every operating tab.","The framing now follows Bitcoin from an unknown hobby project through market discovery, industrialisation, sovereign stress and institutional adoption.","Late-game copy presents Bitcoin as a scarce, permissionless escape valve from fiat and counterparty risk without treating that thesis as guaranteed." ]},
  {date:"2026-08-09",title:"Nodes, templates and audit trail",items:["Added OCEAN and miner-selected block-template technology.","Added pruned, archival and mining-relay node profiles with power, bandwidth, connectivity and mining effects.","Established this permanent collapsed changelog in the Method tab."]},
  {date:"2026-08-09",title:"Historical data calibration",items:["Stored 118 Coin Metrics BTC/USD observations directly in the offline game.","Expanded network hashrate to 69 stored anchors and calibrated recent pool shares from mempool.space.","Added MARA Pool, Luxor, OCEAN and SpiderPool to recent pool history."]},
  {date:"2026-08-09",title:"Progression, finance and energy",items:["Added the Bitcoin whitepaper as the first learning activity.","Future content stays hidden until its announcement window.","Changed project finance to fiat-only collateral and strengthened energy, utilisation and contract trade-offs."]}
];

const MILESTONES=[
  {id:"coin",label:"First full BTC",blurb:"Self-held wallets crossed a whole bitcoin for the first time.",check:()=>controlled()>=1},
  {id:"uptime",label:"One operating year",blurb:"The fleet logged 365 cumulative days of mining uptime.",check:()=>state.uptimeDays>=365},
  {id:"scale",label:"Petahash operator",blurb:"Installed fleet hashrate passed 1 PH/s.",check:()=>fleet().hash>=1e15},
  {id:"reserve",label:"Six-month cash reserve",blurb:"Unborrowed fiat now covers six months of the full operating and finance bill.",check:()=>reserveMilestoneStatus().ok},
  {id:"exahash",label:"Exahash operator",blurb:"Installed fleet hashrate passed 1 EH/s.",check:()=>fleet().hash>=1e18},
  {id:"fiveyears",label:"Five operating years",blurb:"The fleet logged 1,825 cumulative days of mining uptime.",check:()=>state.uptimeDays>=1825},
  {id:"networth",label:"Seven-figure net worth",blurb:"Mark-to-market net worth passed $1,000,000.",check:()=>netWorth()>=1e6},
  {id:"selfheld",label:"100 BTC self-held",blurb:"Hot and cold wallets combined now hold 100 BTC.",check:()=>controlled()>=100},
  {id:"rescued",label:"Survived a restructuring",blurb:"The operation came through a receivership rescue and kept running.",check:()=>state.operator.restructures>=1},
  {id:"centurion",label:"A century of mining",blurb:"The campaign reached the 100-year procedural horizon.",check:()=>state.time>=SANDBOX_END}
];
const EVENTS=[
  {id:"genesis",date:"2009-01-03",title:"The Genesis Block",dek:"A monetary experiment begins with a newspaper headline embedded in block zero.",body:"No market exists — the game's own BTC/USD price stays dark until mid-2010 too — and hashing is tiny, the software is rough, and the network is an idea shared by a handful of people.",cat:"network",imp:3,src:"Bitcoin whitepaper",url:"https://bitcoin.org/bitcoin.pdf"},
  {id:"runningbitcoin",date:"2009-01-11",title:"\"Running bitcoin.\"",dek:"Cypherpunk Hal Finney posts the earliest public words about the software actually working.",body:"It is a small, technical remark from a well-known cryptography veteran — but it is the first public evidence that Bitcoin already had a second participant beyond its pseudonymous creator.",cat:"network",imp:2,src:"Bitcoin Wiki",url:"https://en.bitcoin.it/wiki/Hal_Finney"},
  {id:"firsttx",date:"2009-01-12",title:"The first transaction",dek:"Satoshi sends 10 BTC to Hal Finney in block 170 — the first payment between two people.",body:"The genesis block proved the software could run; this proves value could actually move between independent parties. Every later transaction on the network repeats this same small act.",cat:"network",imp:2,src:"Bitcoin Wiki",url:"https://en.bitcoin.it/wiki/Block_170"},
  {id:"firstprice",date:"2009-10-05",title:"A first price, of sorts",dek:"Someone finally puts a number on it: roughly 1,309 BTC per dollar, based on the electricity it cost to mine them.",body:"It is less a market than an educated guess — there is barely a buyer or seller in sight — but it is the first attempt to price the network in a currency everyone already understood.",cat:"markets",imp:1,src:"Bitcoin Wiki",url:"https://en.bitcoin.it/wiki/History"},
  {id:"bitcointalk",date:"2009-11-22",title:"A forum for the forming community",dek:"Development chatter and mining tips move to a dedicated message board.",body:"For years this is where protocol changes, exchange rates and hardware advice get argued out in public — a rare direct line into a still-tiny, mostly anonymous community.",cat:"network",imp:1,src:"BitcoinTalk",url:"https://bitcointalk.org/"},
  {id:"subreddit",date:"2010-11-25",title:"r/Bitcoin finds its crowd",dek:"A subreddit gives the community a faster, louder gathering point than the forum.",body:"Price chatter, technical debate and no shortage of the network's earliest running jokes find a home here — a sign Bitcoin's audience is starting to outgrow one technical forum.",cat:"adoption",imp:1,src:"Reddit",url:"https://www.reddit.com/r/Bitcoin/"},
  {id:"satoshigone",date:"2010-12-12",title:"Satoshi's last known message",dek:"Bitcoin's pseudonymous creator mentions moving on to other things, then goes quiet.",body:"No protocol change marks the moment; the software keeps running exactly as designed. It becomes the clearest proof yet that Bitcoin does not depend on any one person staying in charge of it.",cat:"network",imp:3,src:"Bitcoin Wiki",url:"https://en.bitcoin.it/wiki/Satoshi_Nakamoto"},
  {id:"wiredprofile",date:"2011-11-23",title:"A national magazine takes notice",dek:"Wired runs a long profile chasing Bitcoin's mystery, its money and the hunt for Satoshi.",body:"Coverage like this carries Bitcoin out of forums and mailing lists and into a mainstream audience that had never heard of it — for better and worse, once Silk Road becomes part of the same story.",cat:"adoption",imp:2,src:"Wired",url:"https://www.wired.com/"},
  {id:"overflow",date:"2010-08-15",title:"The value-overflow bug is contained",dek:"An invalid transaction creates an impossible quantity of bitcoin; the network rolls back through an emergency upgrade.",body:"The episode is an early lesson in the value of many people independently running and reviewing software. Consensus is resilient, but implementation bugs still matter.",cat:"network",imp:1,src:"Bitcoin Wiki",url:"https://en.bitcoin.it/wiki/Value_overflow_incident"},
  {id:"pizza",date:"2010-05-22",title:"Two pizzas, 10,000 BTC",dek:"Bitcoin crosses from abstract units into a memorable real-world exchange.",body:"The purchase becomes a cultural price-discovery milestone. Liquidity remains almost nonexistent.",cat:"markets",imp:2,src:"Bitcoin Wiki",url:"https://en.bitcoin.it/wiki/Laszlo_Hanyecz"},
  {id:"mtgoxopen",date:"2010-07-17",title:"Continuous trading arrives",dek:"Mt. Gox becomes the dominant early venue and gives Bitcoin a visible dollar price — and its balance sheet, not yours, now holds the keys to whatever you deposit.",body:"The convenience is transformative, and so is the concentration of counterparty risk: in this game, anything left on a venue counts as custodial BTC, not self-held bitcoin, until you withdraw it to a wallet you control.",cat:"custody",imp:3,src:"Mt. Gox rehabilitation",url:"https://www.mtgox.com/"},
  {id:"parity",date:"2011-02-09",title:"Bitcoin reaches dollar parity",dek:"For the first time, one bitcoin trades around one U.S. dollar.",body:"The number is small, but it makes the experiment legible to a much wider audience and gives miners a clearer economic signal.",cat:"markets",imp:1,src:"Bitcoin Wiki",url:"https://en.bitcoin.it/wiki/History"},
  {id:"silk",date:"2011-02-01",title:"Censorship resistance meets the dark web",dek:"Silk Road creates demand and draws intense scrutiny.",body:"Bitcoin becomes entangled with a geopolitical argument about borders, surveillance and illicit finance that will follow it for years.",cat:"policy",imp:2,src:"U.S. Department of Justice",url:"https://www.justice.gov/usao-sdny/pr/ross-ulbricht-creator-and-owner-silk-road-website-found-guilty-manhattan-federal-court"},
  {id:"wikileaksdonate",date:"2011-06-14",title:"WikiLeaks turns to Bitcoin donations",dek:"A publisher cut off from conventional payment rails accepts Bitcoin support.",body:"The episode becomes an early proof that Bitcoin can move value when conventional intermediaries refuse service.",cat:"civil society",imp:2,src:"WikiLeaks",url:"https://wikileaks.org/donate.html"},
  {id:"halving1",date:"2012-11-28",title:"The first halving",dek:"New supply per block falls from 50 BTC to 25 BTC.",body:"The schedule works exactly as coded. In the game's own payout formula, expected BTC/day is blocks × (subsidy + fees) — halving the subsidy overnight cuts miner revenue immediately, and inefficient hardware feels it first.",cat:"network",imp:3,src:"Bitcoin developer reference",url:"https://developer.bitcoin.org/reference/block_chain.html"},
  {id:"foundation",date:"2012-09-27",title:"The Bitcoin Foundation forms",dek:"Early industry participants create an advocacy and standards-oriented organisation.",body:"It reflects Bitcoin's growing public profile and the recurring tension between informal open-source coordination and representative institutions.",cat:"network",imp:1,src:"Bitcoin Foundation archive",url:"https://en.bitcoin.it/wiki/Bitcoin_Foundation"},
  {id:"fincen",date:"2013-03-18",title:"Washington defines the perimeter",dek:"FinCEN issues guidance for virtual-currency businesses.",body:"Bitcoin is no longer too small for formal financial regulation. Compliance becomes part of the infrastructure.",cat:"policy",imp:2,src:"FinCEN",url:"https://www.fincen.gov/resources/statutes-regulations/guidance/application-fincens-regulations-persons-administering"},
  {id:"cyprus",date:"2013-03-25",title:"Cyprus and the bank bail-in",dek:"Capital controls and losses for uninsured depositors sharpen the case for assets outside banks.",body:"Bitcoin rallies during the crisis, but the exact causal contribution remains debated — the same distinction every event card in this game draws: a price move shown as context, never as proof. The event becomes part of Bitcoin's political mythology regardless.",cat:"geopolitics",imp:3,src:"European Commission",url:"https://economy-finance.ec.europa.eu/eu-financial-assistance/euro-area-countries/financial-assistance-cyprus_en"},
  {id:"silkseized",date:"2013-10-02",title:"The Silk Road is seized",dek:"U.S. authorities shut the marketplace and seize a vast hoard of bitcoin.",body:"The network continues. The state demonstrates that Bitcoin is censorship-resistant infrastructure, not immunity from law enforcement.",cat:"geopolitics",imp:3,src:"U.S. Department of Justice",url:"https://www.justice.gov/usao-sdny/pr/manhattan-us-attorney-announces-seizure-additional-28-million-worth-bitcoins-belonging"},
  {id:"china13",date:"2013-12-05",title:"China restricts financial institutions",dek:"The People's Bank of China warns institutions away from Bitcoin business.",body:"Policy risk in the world's most important mining and trading region becomes a recurring market force.",cat:"geopolitics",imp:3,src:"People's Bank of China",url:"https://www.pbc.gov.cn/english/130721/2013/index.html"},
  {id:"mtgox",date:"2014-02-24",title:"Mt. Gox goes dark",dek:"The largest early exchange suspends trading and enters bankruptcy.",body:"Bitcoin does not live on an exchange; an exchange holds keys on a customer's behalf. The game scores only self-held hot and cold BTC — anyone who left their balance on Mt. Gox learned that distinction the hardest way possible.",cat:"custody",imp:3,src:"Mt. Gox rehabilitation",url:"https://www.mtgox.com/",fx:"mtgox"},
  {id:"auction",date:"2014-06-27",title:"The U.S. auctions seized bitcoin",dek:"A government sale turns confiscated coins into an institutional asset lot.",body:"States may prosecute Bitcoin-enabled crime while treating the asset itself as saleable property.",cat:"geopolitics",imp:2,src:"U.S. Department of Justice",url:"https://www.justice.gov/usao-sdny/pr/acting-manhattan-us-attorney-announces-forfeiture-48-million-sale-silk-road-bitcoins"},
  {id:"bitlicense",date:"2015-06-03",title:"New York's BitLicense",dek:"A major financial centre creates a dedicated licensing regime.",body:"Consumer protection and compliance arrive with consolidation: smaller operators face costs they cannot absorb.",cat:"policy",imp:2,src:"New York DFS",url:"https://www.dfs.ny.gov/virtual_currency_businesses"},
  {id:"halving2",date:"2016-07-09",title:"The second halving",dek:"The subsidy falls to 12.5 BTC.",body:"Mining economics tighten again: the same subsidy term in your expected-BTC/day formula is cut in half, rewarding scale and efficient silicon over brute machine count.",cat:"network",imp:3,src:"Bitcoin developer reference",url:"https://developer.bitcoin.org/reference/block_chain.html"},
  {id:"bitfinexhack",date:"2016-08-02",title:"Bitfinex is hacked",dek:"A major exchange loses roughly 120,000 BTC and socialises losses across customer balances.",body:"The venue continues operating, but custody convenience comes with a reminder: exchange balances are claims exposed to the operator's security model, and in this game they sit in custodial BTC, not the self-held total that counts toward your final score.",cat:"custody",imp:3,src:"Bitfinex security incident",url:"https://www.bitfinex.com/posts/213",fx:"bitfinex"},
  {id:"winklevossetfdenied",date:"2017-03-10",title:"The first Winklevoss ETF bid is denied",dek:"The SEC rejects the proposed rule change that would have listed the Winklevoss Bitcoin Trust.",body:"First proposed in 2013, the trust is rejected four years later: regulators say the exchange hasn't shown adequate protection against fraud and manipulation in the underlying bitcoin market. Wall Street access will have to wait.",cat:"markets",imp:2,src:"U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission",url:"https://www.sec.gov/files/rules/sro/batsbzx/2017/34-80206.pdf"},
  {id:"japan",date:"2017-04-01",title:"Japan recognises Bitcoin payments",dek:"A national framework pulls exchanges into regulation.",body:"Recognition broadens access while making custody businesses more legible to the state.",cat:"policy",imp:2,src:"Japan Financial Services Agency",url:"https://www.fsa.go.jp/en/policy/virtual_currency/index.html"},
  {id:"segwit",date:"2017-08-24",title:"SegWit activates",dek:"A major soft fork changes how transaction data is structured and expands effective block capacity.",body:"The upgrade improves transaction malleability handling and opens a path for second-layer designs. It is also a landmark in Bitcoin's decentralised governance story.",cat:"network",imp:2,src:"Bitcoin Optech",url:"https://bitcoinops.org/en/topics/segwit/"},
  {id:"china17",date:"2017-09-04",title:"China closes the trading door",dek:"Authorities move against ICOs and domestic crypto exchanges.",body:"Trading migrates offshore. Mining remains concentrated in China, leaving the network — and any in-game facility still sitting in an exposed region — vulnerable to the policy break that follows four years later.",cat:"geopolitics",imp:3,src:"People's Bank of China",url:"https://www.pbc.gov.cn/english/130721/3131759/index.html"},
  {id:"futures",date:"2017-12-17",title:"Bitcoin futures reach CME",dek:"A systemically important derivatives venue launches regulated futures.",body:"Institutional access expands, including the ability to express a short view.",cat:"markets",imp:2,src:"CME Group",url:"https://www.cmegroup.com/media-room/press-releases/2017/12/17/cme_group_self-certifiesbitcoinfuturestolaunchdec18.html"},
  {id:"lightningmainnet",date:"2018-03-15",title:"Lightning reaches mainnet beta",dek:"A payment network built on Bitcoin begins its cautious public rollout.",body:"Lightning promises faster, lower-value payments without putting every transfer directly on-chain. In the game it arrives from 2018 as routing liquidity — lock hot-wallet BTC into channels to earn a small daily fee, with an online archival or relay node required to keep it running.",cat:"network",imp:2,src:"Lightning Labs",url:"https://lightning.engineering/posts/2018-03-15-lightning-mainnet-beta"},
  {id:"whitepaper10",date:"2018-10-31",title:"Ten years of the whitepaper",dek:"Bitcoin's founding paper reaches a decade in circulation.",body:"The system has moved from an obscure proposal to a global market, while its original questions about money, trust and self-custody remain active.",cat:"network",imp:1,src:"Bitcoin whitepaper",url:"https://bitcoin.org/bitcoin.pdf"},
  {id:"quadriga",date:"2019-02-05",title:"QuadrigaCX collapses",dek:"Canada's largest exchange is unable to return customer assets after the death of its founder and a severe custody shortfall.",body:"Users learn again that a balance on an exchange is not the same thing as bitcoin controlled by your own keys — exactly the line this game draws between self-held hot and cold wallets and everything else.",cat:"custody",imp:3,src:"Ontario Securities Commission",url:"https://www.osc.ca/en/news-events/news/osc-concludes-investigation-quadrigacx-and-its-founder-gerald-cotten",fx:"quadriga"},
  {id:"covid",date:"2020-03-12",title:"The global dash for cash",dek:"As COVID-19 shocks markets, Bitcoin falls with nearly every liquid risk asset.",body:"The crisis punctures the idea that Bitcoin is always an immediate safe haven, and the same shock ripples into the game's spare-parts market: lead times stretch to 42 days and prices jump 2.25× until mid-2021, so a fleet already due for service gets harder to keep running.",cat:"geopolitics",imp:3,src:"World Health Organization",url:"https://www.who.int/europe/emergencies/situations/covid-19"},
  {id:"halving3",date:"2020-05-11",title:"The third halving",dek:"The subsidy falls to 6.25 BTC amid extraordinary monetary expansion.",body:"The contrast between fixed issuance and discretionary policy becomes Bitcoin's dominant macro story — and in-game, every miner's expected daily BTC drops with the subsidy, regardless of how much fiat was spent on hardware.",cat:"network",imp:3,src:"Bitcoin developer reference",url:"https://developer.bitcoin.org/reference/block_chain.html"},
  {id:"paypal",date:"2020-10-21",title:"PayPal brings Bitcoin to its users",dek:"A global payments company launches buying, holding and selling of cryptocurrency for eligible customers.",body:"Access broadens dramatically, even as the custodial model reminds users that an account balance is different from keys and direct settlement.",cat:"markets",imp:2,src:"PayPal",url:"https://newsroom.paypal-corp.com/2020-10-21-PayPal-Launches-a-New-Service-Enabling-Users-to-Buy-Hold-and-Sell-Cryptocurrency"},
  {id:"tesla",date:"2021-02-08",title:"Bitcoin enters a corporate treasury",dek:"Tesla discloses a $1.5 billion purchase and plans to accept bitcoin.",body:"A public company turns a fringe treasury strategy into a boardroom question worldwide — the same corporate Bitcoin-treasury bet that Strategy's fiat-priced securities in this game's Market tab exist to proxy.",cat:"markets",imp:3,src:"U.S. SEC filing",url:"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1318605/000156459021004599/tsla-10k_20201231.htm"},
  {id:"elsalvador",date:"2021-06-09",title:"El Salvador makes Bitcoin legal tender",dek:"A sovereign state puts Bitcoin into national law.",body:"The experiment expands Bitcoin's geopolitical role and triggers debate over adoption, coercion, remittances and sovereign risk.",cat:"geopolitics",imp:3,src:"El Salvador Legislative Assembly",url:"https://www.asamblea.gob.sv/node/11282"},
  {id:"chinaexit",date:"2021-06-21",title:"China expels the miners",dek:"Provincial shutdowns drive the largest geographic migration in proof-of-work history.",body:"Network hash rate collapses, then recovers elsewhere. Cheap power is worthless when political permission disappears — the same relocation risk the game models whenever a facility moves into or out of an exposed region.",cat:"geopolitics",imp:3,src:"People's Bank of China",url:"https://www.pbc.gov.cn/en/3688253/3689012/4353814/index.html",fx:"china"},
  {id:"riottexas",date:"2021-08-01",title:"A Texas miner grows grid-sized",dek:"Riot Platforms' build-out at its Rockdale facility becomes large enough to be a genuine factor in ERCOT's regional power balance.",body:"Texas courted Bitcoin miners as flexible, curtailable load; Riot's own scale-up is one of the clearest examples of that bet paying off for the grid operator during tight periods — and a reminder that any facility sharing that grid, yours included, will feel the same regional price pressure when demand spikes.",cat:"markets",imp:2,src:"ERCOT",url:"https://www.ercot.com/",fx:"riotx"},
  {id:"taproot",date:"2021-11-14",title:"Taproot activates",dek:"A privacy- and efficiency-oriented soft fork reaches the network after a broad signalling process.",body:"The upgrade expands the design space for complex spending conditions while making many of them look more like ordinary transactions on-chain.",cat:"network",imp:2,src:"Bitcoin Optech",url:"https://bitcoinops.org/en/topics/taproot/"},
  {id:"kazakh",date:"2022-01-05",title:"Kazakhstan goes dark",dek:"Unrest and a nationwide internet shutdown hit a major post-China mining hub.",body:"Geographic diversification helped the network, but miners who chased one cheap grid discovered a new concentration risk — the same connectivity-outage exposure the game prices into every region's jurisdiction risk.",cat:"geopolitics",imp:2,src:"Internet Society",url:"https://pulse.internetsociety.org/shutdowns/internet-shutdown-in-kazakhstan",fx:"kazakh"},
  {id:"ukraine",date:"2022-02-24",title:"War tests borderless money",dek:"Russia invades Ukraine; sanctions, donations and capital controls put crypto rails under scrutiny.",body:"Bitcoin is used by donors and individuals while governments focus on sanctions enforcement. The same neutrality serves conflicting human purposes.",cat:"geopolitics",imp:3,src:"European Council",url:"https://www.consilium.europa.eu/en/policies/eu-response-ukraine-invasion/"},
  {id:"ukrdonate",date:"2022-02-26",title:"Ukraine opens crypto donation channels",dek:"Public crypto addresses become part of a rapid global fundraising effort.",body:"The moment shows both the speed and transparency trade-offs of borderless donations during a humanitarian and military emergency.",cat:"civil society",imp:2,src:"Ukraine digital aid",url:"https://donate.thedigital.gov.ua/"},
  {id:"useo",date:"2022-03-09",title:"A whole-of-government U.S. strategy",dek:"The White House orders agencies to coordinate digital-asset policy.",body:"Bitcoin is now a matter of consumer protection, competitiveness, illicit finance, energy and national security at once.",cat:"policy",imp:2,src:"White House archive",url:"https://bidenwhitehouse.archives.gov/briefing-room/presidential-actions/2022/03/09/executive-order-on-ensuring-responsible-development-of-digital-assets/"},
  {id:"terra",date:"2022-05-12",title:"Leverage unwinds",dek:"The Terra ecosystem collapses and forced selling spreads through crypto markets.",body:"Bitcoin keeps producing blocks, but the credit system built around digital assets proves deeply connected and fragile.",cat:"markets",imp:2,src:"Federal Reserve",url:"https://www.federalreserve.gov/publications/november-2022-financial-stability-report-digital-assets.htm"},
  {id:"merge",date:"2022-09-15",title:"Ethereum leaves proof-of-work",dek:"Ethereum completes its transition to proof-of-stake, making Bitcoin's proof-of-work model stand out more sharply.",body:"The contrast reframes energy debates: Bitcoin miners face more scrutiny, but also a clearer opportunity to demonstrate flexible demand and grid services.",cat:"network",imp:1,src:"Ethereum Foundation",url:"https://ethereum.org/en/roadmap/merge/"},
  {id:"computenorthbankrupt",date:"2022-09-22",title:"Compute North files for bankruptcy",dek:"A major U.S. mining host collapses under its own expansion debt, pushing a wave of hosted ASICs onto the resale market.",body:"Compute North grew fast on borrowed money and cheap power deals; when both tightened at once, Chapter 11 followed. Displaced hosting clients and secured creditors alike start moving hardware, and the in-game secondary ASIC market gets measurably cheaper for a few months.",cat:"markets",imp:2,src:"U.S. Bankruptcy Court, Southern District of Texas",url:"https://www.reuters.com/business/energy/bitcoin-miner-compute-north-files-bankruptcy-2022-09-22/",fx:"computenorthx"},
  {id:"ftx",date:"2022-11-11",title:"FTX files for bankruptcy",dek:"A globally prominent exchange fails with an enormous customer shortfall.",body:"Proof of reserves, segregation and self-custody return to the centre of the debate. Reputation is not the same thing as solvency — and a balance you haven't withdrawn is a claim on the venue's solvency, not bitcoin you hold.",cat:"custody",imp:3,src:"U.S. Department of Justice",url:"https://www.justice.gov/opa/pr/samuel-bankman-fried-sentenced-25-years-his-orchestration-multiple-fraudulent-schemes",fx:"ftx"},
  {id:"corescientificbankrupt",date:"2022-12-21",title:"Core Scientific files for Chapter 11",dek:"One of the largest publicly traded Bitcoin miners in the U.S. seeks bankruptcy protection.",body:"A punishing mix of falling BTC prices, a strong dollar and heavy equipment debt catches up with one of the sector's biggest names. The resulting liquidation adds even more secondhand ASICs to a market already softened by Compute North's collapse months earlier.",cat:"markets",imp:3,src:"U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission",url:"https://www.sec.gov/cgi-bin/browse-edgar?action=getcompany&CIK=CORZ",fx:"corescix"},
  {id:"banks",date:"2023-03-10",title:"A banking crisis hits crypto's rails",dek:"Silicon Valley Bank fails after Silvergate winds down; access to dollars tightens.",body:"Bitcoin rallies as bank fragility revives its origin story, even while crypto firms lose critical banking infrastructure.",cat:"markets",imp:3,src:"Federal Reserve review",url:"https://www.federalreserve.gov/publications/review-of-the-federal-reserves-supervision-and-regulation-of-silicon-valley-bank.htm"},
  {id:"ordinals",date:"2023-01-21",title:"Inscriptions reshape the fee market",dek:"Ordinal inscriptions bring new kinds of data and demand to Bitcoin block space.",body:"The debate is immediate: permissionless block space can invite unexpected uses, and miners gain another reminder that transaction fees — the second term in every block's payout, alongside the subsidy — may matter more over time.",cat:"network",imp:2,src:"Ordinals",url:"https://ordinals.com/"},
  {id:"mica",date:"2023-05-16",title:"Europe adopts MiCA",dek:"The EU creates a bloc-wide framework for crypto-asset services.",body:"Regulatory clarity can increase compliance cost and institutional confidence at the same time.",cat:"policy",imp:2,src:"Council of the EU",url:"https://www.consilium.europa.eu/en/press/press-releases/2023/05/16/digital-finance-council-adopts-new-rules-on-markets-in-crypto-assets-mica/"},
  {id:"binance",date:"2023-11-21",title:"Binance settles U.S. criminal charges",dek:"The world's largest crypto exchange agrees to major penalties and compliance commitments.",body:"The case reinforces a durable lesson for the player: liquidity venues are businesses with legal, operational and counterparty risk — not neutral extensions of the protocol, and not the self-held BTC the game scores at the end of a run.",cat:"custody",imp:2,src:"U.S. Department of Justice",url:"https://www.justice.gov/opa/pr/binance-and-its-ceo-plead-guilty-federal-charges"},
  {id:"etf",date:"2024-01-10",title:"U.S. spot Bitcoin products approved",dek:"The SEC approves exchange rules for spot Bitcoin ETPs.",body:"Brokerage accounts gain price exposure at scale. An ETF is not self-custodied bitcoin and cannot validate or transact on the network — in the game's own header it sits in illiquid fiat, not the self-held BTC that counts toward your score.",cat:"markets",imp:3,src:"U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission",url:"https://www.sec.gov/newsroom/speeches-statements/gensler-statement-spot-bitcoin-011023",fx:"etf"},
  {id:"halving4",date:"2024-04-19",title:"The fourth halving",dek:"The subsidy falls to 3.125 BTC as fee-market experiments intensify.",body:"Every miner now competes for half the new issuance available a day earlier — check your mining-share economics now, since the subsidy component of your payout has just halved again.",cat:"network",imp:3,src:"Bitcoin developer reference",url:"https://developer.bitcoin.org/reference/block_chain.html"},
  {id:"mtgoxrepay",date:"2024-07-05",title:"Mt. Gox repayments begin",dek:"After a decade of insolvency proceedings, distributions to former customers finally start.",body:"The long aftermath is a sobering capstone to the early-exchange era: custody failures can outlast multiple market cycles — a reminder that the safest time to withdraw a venue balance was always before the failure, not after.",cat:"custody",imp:1,src:"Mt. Gox rehabilitation",url:"https://www.mtgox.com/"},
  {id:"policy25",date:"2025-01-23",title:"Washington changes direction",dek:"A new executive order promotes U.S. leadership in digital assets and revokes the 2022 order.",body:"The regulatory pendulum becomes a market variable in its own right.",cat:"geopolitics",imp:3,src:"The White House",url:"https://www.whitehouse.gov/presidential-actions/2025/01/strengthening-american-leadership-in-digital-financial-technology/"},
  {id:"realbedford",date:"2025-02-20",title:"The Winklevoss twins buy into Real Bedford",dek:"Winklevoss Capital finalises a $4.5 million investment for a 45% stake in the non-league football club.",body:"Eight years after their Bitcoin ETF was rejected, Cameron and Tyler Winklevoss become co-owners of Peter McCormack's Real Bedford FC. Bitcoin's institutional era now includes a very literal attempt to climb the English football pyramid.",cat:"adoption",imp:1,src:"Sky Sports and Companies House",url:"https://www.skysports.com/football/news/11095/13312885/real-bedford-fc-cryptocurrency-investors-cameron-and-tyler-winklevoss-inject-gbp3-58m-and-become-part-owners"},
  {id:"reserve",date:"2025-03-06",title:"The United States establishes a Bitcoin reserve",dek:"An executive order directs forfeited government BTC into a Strategic Bitcoin Reserve.",body:"The asset once seized mainly as criminal proceeds is recast as a strategic state holding. Sovereign game theory is no longer hypothetical.",cat:"geopolitics",imp:3,src:"The White House",url:"https://www.whitehouse.gov/presidential-actions/2025/03/establishment-of-the-strategic-bitcoin-reserve-and-united-states-digital-asset-stockpile/"},
  {id:"inkind",date:"2025-07-29",title:"Crypto ETPs gain in-kind mechanics",dek:"The SEC permits in-kind creations and redemptions for crypto exchange-traded products.",body:"Market plumbing becomes more efficient, but retail ETF holders still own shares rather than spendable bitcoin.",cat:"markets",imp:2,src:"U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission",url:"https://www.sec.gov/newsroom/speeches-statements/uyeda-statement-crypto-exchange-traded-products-072925"},
  {id:"framework26",date:"2026-05-18",title:"Digital assets enter the regulatory framework",dek:"The U.S. pushes digital-asset market structure deeper into mainstream financial policy.",body:"Bitcoin's story has travelled from a mailing list to state balance sheets and national regulatory architecture. The protocol still settles blocks on its own clock.",cat:"geopolitics",imp:3,src:"The White House",url:"https://www.whitehouse.gov/fact-sheets/2026/05/fact-sheet-president-donald-j-trump-integrates-financial-technology-innovation-into-regulatory-frameworks/"}
];
const EXPOSURE_WARNINGS=[
  {id:"mtgoxwarn",eventId:"mtgox",date:"2014-02-07",wallet:"mtgox",title:"Mt. Gox halts bitcoin withdrawals",body:"Mt. Gox has stopped all BTC withdrawals, blaming a technical bug it calls transaction malleability. The exchange says it's temporary."},
  {id:"quadrigawarn",eventId:"quadriga",date:"2018-10-09",wallet:"quadriga",title:"A bank has frozen QuadrigaCX's funds",body:"CIBC has frozen roughly C$28M tied to QuadrigaCX's payment processor, and a court has been asked to decide who owns it."},
  {id:"ftxwarn",eventId:"ftx",date:"2022-11-02",wallet:"frontier",title:"Questions raised over a major exchange's finances",body:"Leaked documents suggest a large share of a sister trading firm's balance sheet is the exchange's own token, not independent assets."},
  {id:"chinawarn",eventId:"chinaexit",date:"2021-05-21",region:"sichuan",title:"Beijing calls to crack down on mining",body:"China's top financial regulator has singled out Bitcoin mining and trading for the first time. Provincial power cuts could follow fast."}
];
